.TH "libnvmf_owner_equal" 9 "libnvmf_owner_equal" "November 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvmf_owner_equal \- Compare two registry owners
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "bool" libnvmf_owner_equal
.BI "(const char *a "  ","
.BI "const char *b "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "a" 12
Owner, or NULL for no owner
.IP "b" 12
Owner, or NULL for no owner
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
The pre-OS environment (firmware and initrd) records the owner "pre-os".
Its old name "nbft", which initrds with older nvme-cli still record, is
the same owner.
.SH "RETURN"
true if \fIa\fP and \fIb\fP name the same owner, or both are NULL.
